       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it would give 6,000 mg of acetaminophen per day. That's well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 2,000 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. Even with normal liver and kidney function, this carries a real risk of hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some options that would fit the usual limits:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily**, every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day, the standard maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf 2,000 mg TID is intentional, for example because of a protocol I don't know about or a typo in the frequency or dose, tell me and I'll enter it with that noted. Otherwise, tell me which of the options above you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
